suggestions.suggestionContent:
checkHistogram's search loop keeps `foundLabels` outside the per-metric loop and never resets it, and a partially-matching metric aborts the entire function instead of continuing to the next candidate. The helper implicitly assumes the first metric with at least one matching label is the target: with a multi-metric family, a metric whose `plugin_id` matches but whose `endpoint`/`target` differs triggers the immediate `return fmt.Errorf("expected label %q ...")` (or, for subset-matching metrics, the `foundLabels != len(expLabels)` error with a counter polluted by the previous metric), so a fully-matching metric later in the family is never found and callers using require.NoError fail spuriously. It only works today because each metric family in this test happens to contain exactly one metric. Reset the match state per metric and skip non-matching metrics instead of returning an error:

```go
var metric *dto.Metric
for _, m := range metricFamily.Metric {
	foundLabels := 0
	match := true
	for _, l := range m.GetLabel() {
		v, ok := expLabels[*l.Name]
		if !ok {
			continue
		}
		if v != *l.Value {
			match = false
			break
		}
		foundLabels++
	}
	if match && foundLabels == len(expLabels) {
		metric = m
		break
	}
}
```
